Z||000004||AkursedX||12-12-2001||12:50 PM||||Hmmmm....if you don't want to go turbo or NOS, then to getthe most power out of your 2.8, you would have to.....<P>Get the crank knifedged and polished.<BR>Get some forged aluminum SBC connecting rods.<BR>High compression forged aluminium pistons.<BR>A nice hi-po cam, lots of choices.<BR>hi-po lifters and pushrods<BR>stainless steel valves<BR>titanium valve springs<BR>1.6:1 full roller rockers<BR>Heads fully ported and a nice valve job<BR>TB upper, middle, and lower intake all ported and extrude-honed<BR>cold-air intake<BR>full length headers<BR>borla exhaust<BR>Power pullies<BR>MSD 6A box<BR>Big wires and hi-po sparkplugs<P>That's about all I can think of right now.<P>I'm guessing and hoping that will get me around 220 hp, and some serious high rev's.<P>But...it will cost just as much as a v-8 conversion that would get you more power anyways.<P>So dollar/power, an engine swap would be your best choice.  Engine choice is a matter of preference though.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
